            <ArticleTitle>A bizarre giant leiomyoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the clinical and imaging features of a huge deep leiomyoma of the rectus abdominis treated surgically in an 84-year-old man. Hypotheses are put forward to elucidate the etiology of this enigmatic localization, apparently the first described in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
